Is this a real problem?  I don't remember the last time I got greasy
hands, and it lasts only a few turns anyway.  It's not long enough for
me to bother looking up the command and then waste a turn on it,
though I suppose if I was foolish enough to try eating a tin with
adjacent monsters #wipe could be handy.  (FWIW I usually discard all
tins except spinach and those that could give me a useful missing
intrinsic).

>  I've certainly used #wipe more often than
> quit.  I also use A from time to time, when I'm in a safe place,
> and want to try on other armor.

Using T means that you stop automatically between pieces of armor,
which is nice in case a monster comes into view (so you can act before
it walks up and tries to hit you or whatever).  I could see using A in
the circumstances you outline, but I never bothered fighting the 'T'
muscle memory.


